# Defensive exclusions layered on top of the package.json `files` allowlist.
# `files` allowlists whole directories (e.g. `scripts`), and npm does NOT honor
# .gitignore inside an allowlisted dir — so Python bytecode generated by a local
# or CI run (`__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`) could otherwise be globbed into the
# published tarball. The CLI is zero-runtime-dependency shell+python source;
# compiled bytecode must never ship. (ISEDC E09 DR / clean reproducible tarball.)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
